id: decisions/004-when-a-concern-earns-a-record
title: "One split test for when a concern gets its own record"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'record-granularity'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: record-granularity
axis_gloss: "whether one concern gets one small record each, or several concerns are fused into a single larger record"
poles:
  a: decomposed-many-records
  b: combined-single-record
split: genuinely-split
draft_status: full
leverage: 36
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(24) x split_weight(1) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.5)"

question: >
  When does one concern earn its own .yawn — whenever it has a name or an ID, or
  only when its proof, owner, status or rollback would differ from its parent's?

why_it_matters: >
  The repo authors both halves of this: it splits a bot across four files and
  links rather than merges overlapping records, yet refuses one-Yawn-per-message
  and one-Agent-per-viewpoint; meanwhile a working-draft extension sits inside a
  v1 record and a generator sits inside a node defined as checks-only,
  unremarked. Once answered, a child Yawn deciding whether to fork a
  relationship, a desire or a draft into its own file applies one written test
  instead of guessing from precedent.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    17 judgments sit at decomposed-many-records (7 authored) and 7 at
    combined-single-record (3 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave counts a status or version difference alone as forcing a split,
    or only a difference in proof, owner or rollback.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every distinct concern (a relationship, a desire, a draft extension, a
      module, a generator, a move) is its own record, linked from its parent by a
      typed pointer. Embedding a concern that could stand alone is not allowed.
    cost: "Splits objective_holon_extension_0_1 out of core/motivation-and-purpose.yawn, generators out of scripts/node.yawn, and contradicts the authored refusals in examples/conversation-import-routing.yawn and question-packets/orientation-nine.yawn (a stance is not a second Agent; a message ID is not a reason to become a record)."
    risk: "Record count explodes; the folder-node rule (every active folder carries node.yawn) then multiplies too."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "A test that fails when any nested block inside a record carries its own status:, spec_version:, owner: or proof: — today it fails on core/motivation-and-purpose.yawn and would also fail templates/turn.yawn moves, which the repo wants."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0066"
      - "J0141"
      - "J0148"
      - "J0225"
      - "J0366"
      - "J0417"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: A record may hold everything about its subject, including drafts,
      extensions and sub-moves at other statuses. Splitting is the author's
      discretion and needs no stated criterion.
    cost: "Softens core/holarchy.yawn structural_change_rule and examples/merge-split-routing.yawn, whose merge_counterexample was written precisely to stop merges that fuse different proof conditions, owners and rollback scopes."
    risk: "A v1 record carries working-draft content under the v1 label and a validator that trusts the top-level status trusts the draft."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None can enforce discretion; the record would be striking the five split conditions from core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn section 13."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0254"
      - "J0337"
      - "J0363"
      - "J0522"
      - "J0812"
      - "J0882"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: A concern becomes its own record when its proof condition, owner or
      authority, lifecycle status or version, or rollback scope differs from its
      parent's (the five conditions in core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn
      section 13 plus the merge_counterexample in examples/merge-split-routing.yawn,
      written once in core/holarchy.yawn structural_change_rule). Having an ID, a
      message boundary or a viewpoint is never sufficient on its own. Consequences
      named: objective_holon_extension_0_1 (status working-draft inside a v1 record)
      becomes its own record linked from core/motivation-and-purpose.yawn;
      scripts/node.yawn lists generators under a separate generates: key with the
      purpose line corrected. A turn's plural moves stay embedded because each
      carries its own authority_ref by design.
    cost: "One paragraph in core/holarchy.yawn, one new core record, one edit to scripts/node.yawn, pointers from the existing examples to the rule."
    risk: "A status difference alone (draft inside active) may split things Dave wanted read together."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "New tests/record-granularity.test.mjs: fail when a nested block in a .yawn record carries a top-level-style status: whose value differs from the record's own status (today: core/motivation-and-purpose.yawn); and assert every scripts/*.mjs is listed under exactly one of holds: or generates: in scripts/node.yawn (today: generate-inquiry-selection-receipt-v0.1.mjs sits under holds)."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0148"
      - "J0366"
      - "J0363"
      - "J0522"
      - "J0812"
      - "J0882"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.8
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Both sides are authored, but they do not contradict: the decomposed side
    states when to split (five conditions, a merge counterexample with
    proof/owner/rollback), the combined side states when not to (an ID or a
    viewpoint is not a reason). They are two halves of one criterion that no
    single record writes. The two revealed exceptions (a working-draft block
    inside a v1 file; a generator inside a checks node, outcome-attached) both
    fail the criterion once it is written, so they become the named migrations
    rather than a new rule. The turn's plural moves pass it.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "core/holarchy.yawn structural_change_rule states the split criterion once and examples/merge-split-routing.yawn and examples/conversation-import-routing.yawn point at it."
    - "core/motivation-and-purpose.yawn contains no nested block with its own status: working-draft; the extension is its own record linked from the parent."
    - "scripts/node.yawn separates generates: from holds: and its purpose line no longer claims checks-only."
    - "A test in tests/ rejects a nested block whose status differs from its record and passes."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new draft extension is embedded inside a status: active or v1 record after
    ratification and no test fails.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0066"
  - "J0141"
  - "J0148"
  - "J0225"
  - "J0366"
  - "J0417"
  - "J0254"
  - "J0337"
  - "J0363"
  - "J0522"
  - "J0812"
  - "J0882"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
